################################################################################
# APPENDED 2026-10-02 — G6 FIX ROUND F1/F2. NEW KEYS, read these before building.
#
# Fixture below is G6's live shape: a campaign ("Taco Tuesday", face $5.00) with
# 6 scans and ONE MATCHED $30.00 Toast order whose scan_attempts_mirror
# campaign_id is NULL and whose code_id resolves to no qr_codes row — which is
# EVERY row on live data today (D-4, confirmed at mirror.go:370).
#
# moneyDTO gains TWO keys, on every route, always present:
#   unattributed_redeemed        *int
#   unattributed_revenue_cents   *int
# NON-NULL on the period-scoped routes (GET /campaigns, GET /campaigns/{id},
# PATCH /campaigns/{id}, GET /stats/overview) where 0 is a STATED FACT meaning
# "every redemption found its campaign"; NULL on /stats/by rows and totals,
# where a slice has no opinion on a period fact and states the figure as its own
# `unattributed` row instead (so never sum these across rows).
#
# 🛑 WHAT CARD 2 AND CARD 5 MUST RENDER WHEN IT FIRES (unattributed_redeemed > 0):
#   Card 2 (campaigns money strip, already shipped): the campaign's own
#     revenue_cents IS a true zero — render $0.00 — but it must NOT stand alone.
#     Add a note beside the strip, e.g. "1 redemption ($30.00) not attributed to
#     any campaign" from unattributed_redeemed + unattributed_revenue_cents. A
#     bare $0.00 on this shape is the defect G6 found.
#   Card 5 (stats): the by-campaign slice already carries an `unattributed` ROW
#     with those figures — render it as a real row, never filter it out, or the
#     slice stops summing to the overview.
#
# StatsReconciliation gains THREE keys (the rate now carries its own arithmetic):
#   orphan_rate_basis  "unmatched_and_orphans_excl_duplicate_scan"
#   orphan_numerator   int
#   orphan_denominator int
# 🛑 THE RULE IS UNCHANGED — D-5 is PARKED at top severity on whether the
# UNMATCHED bucket (order number typed, no Toast match) belongs in the numerator.
# Render the basis string somewhere a manager can see it (a tooltip on the orphan
# rate is enough); if the basis string you receive is not the one above, the
# definition changed and your label must change with it.
################################################################################

